    "title": "UNC vs Clemson in 2026 ACC Tournament: Tar Heels don't complete comeback",
    "text": "ACCUNC basketball can't complete comeback vs Clemson in ACC tournament Rodd BaxleyFayetteville ObserverMarch 12, 2026Updated March 13, 2026, 12:13 a.m. ETCHARLOTTE — UNC basketball is one and done at the 2026 ACC Tournament. The 19th-ranked Tar Heels lost 80-79 to Clemson in the quarterfinals at Spectrum Center, bowing out in a rough second-half showing against the Tigers. UNC (24-8) trailed by as many as 18 points after halftime and Clemson (23-10) used a strong performance from its bench to fend off the Heels and earn a spot against Duke (30-2) in the semifinals. The Tigers outscored UNC 29-5 in bench points and iced the game with free throws. UNC was 10 of 17 (59%) from the free-throw line.",
